{"content":"Confirmed: `memopayload.NewRunner` is never called — it's dead code / certified zero. Only `s3presign.NewRunner` is instantiated, and only from `server.go:startBackgroundRunners`.\n\nq28.\n\n**Runners actually started by the server** (`server/server.go`, `startBackgroundRunners`, called from `Server.Start` at server.go:129):\n\n- **s3presign.Runner** — `server/runner/s3presign/runner.go`. Started in `server.go:161-171`: runs once immediately (`s3presignRunner.RunOnce(ctx)`, server.go:163) then loops forever in a goroutine calling `Run(s3Context)` (server.go:167-170). Its own scheduling is a plain `time.Ticker` fired every 12 hours (`runnerInterval = time.Hour * 12`, `server/runner/s3presign/runner.go:27-40`) — re-presigns S3 attachment URLs whose signature is near expiry.\n\nThat is the **only** background runner the server starts. `startBackgroundRunners` (server.go:153-174) creates exactly one cancelable context/goroutine, for s3presign, and nothing else.\n\n**Unused scheduling infrastructure:**\n\n1. **`server/runner/memopayload.Runner`** (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go`) has a full `RunOnce` batch-processing method meant to rebuild all memo payloads, but `memopayload.NewRunner` is never called anywhere in the codebase — confirmed via a certified-zero callers query. Only the plain helper function `memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload` (not the Runner) is used, invoked synchronously inline from `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108` and `:447` during create/update requests — not as a scheduled background job.\n2. **`internal/scheduler`** package — a full cron-style job scheduler (`internal/scheduler/scheduler.go`, `job.go`, `parser.go`, `middleware.go`) with README and tests. `scheduler.New(...)` is referenced only from its own `example_test.go`/`integration_test.go`/`doc.go` — no production code (`cmd/memos/main.go`, `server/server.go`, or any router) imports or constructs it. This entire cron scheduling infrastructure is unused by the running server.","iteration":14,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
